research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:1:{"id":"thm-laurent-cauchy-complete","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"cf72cb0ad7b5762f1d14b7792689e848a473f1fb29fcea5bc9fc6c51998d71cd","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"cc1b09d79aa5ca608eb9ca2a715999b9b4e104e152abd9fcda66a1d06dca64d0","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T10:32:41Z","note":"Terra identifies a real compression in step 2.2, but it closes well inside the binding thirty-second threshold. The cited def-nat-order states verbatim, 'm \\le n \\iff \\exists k \\in \\mathbb{N}\\ (m + k = n)', and the cited thm-induction-principle supplies induction. Induct on that additive gap k: the zero case is reflexivity, and the successor case composes the induction hypothesis with the already proved consecutive inequality using transitivity from thm-nat-linear-order. No predecessor lemma is needed and no mutation is licensed by R1."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:2:{"id":"cex-zero-times-infinity-indeterminate","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"88971447e4b5ec1b6e91a84b63d3fc2707afcb4d086c33a913e8cf697d6d750a","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"c8540f4b61482b0e72b08333b770ac6f4f747c66680519ecc5f909e1b3c40d36","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T10:32:41Z","note":"Terra is right that the phrase 'converge to +\\infty in the extended sense' lacks a direct def-extended-limits citation. The cited def-divergence-to-infinity states verbatim that a sequence 'diverges to $+\\infty$, written $x_k \\to +\\infty$' under the eventual-threshold condition, and step 2.2 proves exactly that condition. The omitted definitional bridge is immediate, and it is not load-bearing: the two constant product limits 1 and 2 already refute the existence of a single v. This is a minor citation quirk, not a fatal mathematical or dependency failure; R1 licenses no edit."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:3:{"id":"cor-convex-subsets-of-rn-are-contractible","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"572661816f4619bae4c4ef7b99ed2d8c453931a7ac4c39f30b27cc6e1de6ee85","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"bb1cce791779ab85da116f724147aed63a1b269df655dfd034a4fbe41580cf38","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T10:32:41Z","note":"The local Fact shortens the cited theorem's hypotheses, but the corollary does not strengthen them: its own Statement begins verbatim, 'Let $n \\ge 1$. Let $C \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^n$ be nonempty and convex'. That standing hypothesis governs the proof, and thm-two-maps-into-a-convex-set-are-homotopic likewise states verbatim, 'Let $n\\ge1$'. A competent reader restores the omitted phrase in seconds; this is nonfatal restatement compression and R1 licenses no edit."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:4:{"id":"lem-straight-line-homotopies-are-continuous","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"470d396a16c5d98e57808029e09842651f4c2b2ac285e0c760823e2347ab726c","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"4421293444a41a1cc2c640107442e57e67780346c1f2c43db34dfb0274765967","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T10:32:41Z","note":"Terra correctly observes that the Statement's formal conclusion is continuity, while the title uses 'homotopy'. The item defines verbatim '$H(x,t):=(1-t)f(x)+t g(x)$'; direct substitution gives H(x,0)=f(x) and H(x,1)=g(x), and the downstream cited theorem records those two equalities explicitly. This one-line endpoint check is below the binding thirty-second threshold and the continuity lemma's stated conclusion is fully proved. R1 licenses no edit."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:5:{"id":"def-the-diagonal-of-a-space","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"64c97dd49e110665cf611de55c274a0bf617fc70ee0bdb337aae1e0b8b4b036b","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"3e4f7f8b63ab058d268723fe7271a80825de167a3e64a47db6999b8e41f0aad7","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T11:16:13Z","note":"Terra identifies a real local hypothesis compression: the pairing is first defined for functions on a bare common domain, while continuity only makes sense after that domain carries a topology. The cited thm-product-universal-property states verbatim, 'For every space $Z$ and every function $h : Z \\to P$', before its continuity equivalence. Thus the final continuity sentence has the immediate conditional reading 'when Z is a topological space'; restoring that four-word hypothesis takes seconds, the bare-set pairing remains well-defined, and R1 licenses no edit."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:6:{"id":"thm-hausdorff-iff-the-diagonal-is-closed","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"590f1a641a9a964a4388e6d9fb8d7512bab7d87d081c94e266effa3c9238f9bf","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"other","item_sha256":"8fea93f9d9d8f98b84203acb65796250a536a6c6908d2766f215d79fe0b87a86","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T11:16:13Z","note":"Terra is correct. The Statement says verbatim, 'every consequence on this page is obtained by pulling $\\Delta_X$ back along a continuous map.' That universal claim is false: the sequence-uniqueness, compact-Hausdorff regularity/normality, and locally-compact-Hausdorff basis results on the same page use direct separation and compactness arguments, not a pullback of the diagonal. This is an explicit false public mathematical scope claim, not a compressed proof step, and licenses a narrow Statement repair."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:7:{"id":"rem-what-the-diagonal-criterion-gives-and-what-it-costs","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"6ddd223bca8659067b7fc139448b3cd647292f0b42da48af1566c4f3f26b848c","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"bfebc1a4aacd425eabdcf839d4928ec7829bcc4751fbd42a39dace093cb32384","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T11:16:13Z","note":"Terra correctly spots an intrinsic-versus-ambient cover compression. The cited def-compact-space says verbatim, 'The last clause speaks about the subspace $(A, \\mathcal{T}_A)$ and its own open sets, not about families of open subsets of the ambient $X$.' Here the fix is immediate from the same cited subspace definition: replace each ambient V by its trace V intersection K, take the finite subcover, then retain the corresponding finitely many original V's. This closes well inside thirty seconds and changes no choice-cost conclusion; R1 licenses no edit."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:8:{"id":"ex-the-graph-of-a-continuous-real-function-is-closed","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"b4c1031b191a621d815a2d61aac6d7151f2b66657b14d8538902ffa080051da7","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"other","item_sha256":"4fe01c8d4499bdbf3f77f1967fceab9b39cda58c39106e9502d8443d6e544269","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T11:16:13Z","note":"Terra is correct. The Remark says verbatim, 'What restores the equivalence is a compact codomain', but the cited theorem states verbatim, 'If $Y$ is compact **and** Hausdorff then $f$ is continuous if and only if $G_f$ is closed'. Compactness alone gives only closed graph implies continuity; the converse still needs Hausdorffness. The omitted hypothesis makes the public Remark false and licenses the one-word fatal repair."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:9:{"id":"ex-a-finite-hausdorff-space-is-discrete","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"cc31e7fbf72c9f0ba6cfd9771592921de824776e1bff3ccb80ad8ddb6d7de117","outcome":"false_positive","item_sha256":"e38f4906c8772f1d5b3b2785e2ad8d2a91bb127977c73f611391282936eb72d5","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T11:16:13Z","note":"Terra overlooks A2's second citation. The cited def-topological-space states verbatim, 'A subset $F \\subseteq X$ is **closed** when its complement $X \\setminus F$ is open'. Step 3.1 applies exactly that definition to the closed complement $X \\setminus A$ established by step 2.1. The inference is explicitly licensed and no edit is permitted."}
research/audit/wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl:10:{"id":"lem-a-locally-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-base-of-open-sets-with-compact-closure","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"920dc89203fc52047ab3bb8a378405f862d25c44e5c70850d891e23a21e6bb59","outcome":"false_positive","item_sha256":"d28d42e619a13f35391c8190033ee0456eaa4295d231f95321394f60dd6c5616","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T11:16:13Z","note":"DeepSeek's source allegation is contradicted by the cited item itself. def-subspace-topology-top states verbatim, 'If $S \\subseteq T \\subseteq X$ then the subspace topology $S$ inherits from $(T, \\mathcal{T}_T)$ is the subspace topology it inherits from $X$'. L1 faithfully repeats that exact transitivity clause, so step 5.1 is licensed and no edit is permitted."}
